{"id":"741f11f5-e7f9-49cb-8237-f3efaec12d03","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The parameter 'args' is an array reference provided for the main method and is never null when run from the command line.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:57.322449Z"}
{"id":"0ac1e0dc-0c81-4d10-9c2b-c350c6908f2b","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The array of arguments is typically expected to be non-null when invoking main, as per Java specification.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:57.322515Z"}
{"id":"d0b6ae1f-9fd8-4ff4-af46-cfbd419ceba1","expr":"b == 0 || b * (a / b) <= a && b * (a / b) >= (a - Math.abs(b) + 1)","rationale":"If b != 0, b * (a / b) provides the largest multiple of b less than or equal to a (for positive b), capturing properties of integer division.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:57.322598Z"}
{"id":"3079dd28-7b3a-424e-8448-ca398370939f","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"Array length in Java is always non-negative, so this must hold for String[] args.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:57.322515Z"}
{"id":"79499980-9690-476c-9589-ba8f03ff3255","expr":"b == 0 || result == a / b","rationale":"If b is 0, we don't perform the division; otherwise, the result is a divided by b.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:57.323473Z"}
{"id":"1f896ad1-d12e-462d-bb21-0cc8ada30bfb","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"An array's length is always non-negative in Java.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:57.322449Z"}
{"id":"84556c78-5366-48fc-9c76-ed7dc0b01d34","expr":"b != 0 || result == Integer.MIN_VALUE","rationale":"If b is 0, the method returns Integer.MIN_VALUE as a designated 'error' value.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:57.323473Z"}
{"id":"79f19152-0be6-45e8-9b87-be2556ac2b5b","expr":"b == 0 || (a / b) * b + a % b == a","rationale":"For b != 0, the division and remainder relationship holds.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:57.322598Z"}
{"id":"8d1942f5-bb06-41a3-a958-f987506eff2c","expr":"b == 0 || result * b == a - (a % b)","rationale":"If b is not 0, result equals a / b; thus, result * b is a - remainder.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:57.323473Z"}
{"id":"470de980-3ccd-4f50-8ff1-eb853050973c","expr":"b != Integer.MIN_VALUE || b != 0","rationale":"b can be Integer.MIN_VALUE or zero, but special care might be required in those extreme values.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:57.322598Z"}
{"id":"8b4a8eae-4c9d-4dd0-b0af-701be29460b9","expr":"b != 0 || result < 0","rationale":"When b is 0, the result is Integer.MIN_VALUE, which is a negative number.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:57.323473Z"}
{"id":"8156eb00-1c72-4b17-9482-a17151ddb787","expr":"Math.abs(result) <= Math.abs(a)","rationale":"The absolute value of the quotient (when b != 0) or the special value is always less than or equal to |a|.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:57.323473Z"}
